# Portal geography + A-M v0 — sandbox

Implementation and exploratory evaluation only. No deployment, schema change,
network requests, production writes or confirmatory holdout use.

## Contents

- `portal_coordinates.patch`: four-file integration candidate against the archived
  Oct 8 production source; not applied outside this sandbox.
- `integration/`: runnable candidate parser, adapter and ingestion pipeline.
- `geo_recovery.py`: archived-detail inventory and encrypted fill-missing plan;
  its writer explicitly accepts SQLite copies only and is idempotent.
- `experimental.py`: local selector using the frozen native A primitives.
- `configurations.json`: fixed 15-profile search; weights remain 40/25/15/10/10.
- `results.json`, `metrics.csv`, `fold_metrics.csv`: aggregate results.
- `*-v2.json.dpapi`: individual predictions and adjustment traces, encrypted for
  the current Windows user. Decrypt in memory using `run.decrypt`; do not export
  plaintext. `backfill_plan.json.dpapi` uses the same protection.

## Geography contract

`Portal map_info.location → MLC-bound raw evidence → existing adapter/cleaner →
Listing coordinates + raw_metadata → repository → Radar / valuation listing`

The existing detail extractor is reused. An already acquired map point can also
be attached with `attach_map_point`; that helper makes no request. Normal cards
without a point remain unchanged. Evidence contains original and normalized
values, publication MLC, source component, parser version, observation timestamp
when supplied, and precision. Unknown acquisition time stays null.

USABLE requires explicit source precision and publication-bound provenance.
UNCERTAIN includes valid unknown/approximate points; these can participate in the
separately flagged experiment. INVALID covers invalid pairs and known conflicts;
MISSING covers no pair. Centroids and coordinates repeated at least five times
are held out of local selection, not deleted. Repetition is measured within
training only in CV. It can also flag a real building; it is a conservative
sensitivity control, not an identity matcher. No source currently establishes
certified exact-address precision. No meter accuracy or polygon validation is
invented. Source publication IDs establish listing association, not physical
property identity.

The SQLite regression verifies ingestion, reobservation, repository mapping and
preservation of a stronger stored point and its provenance. Radar and valuation
repositories share this canonical listing mapping. The production manual Tasar
request/UI does not gain coordinate inputs here: the offline selector receives
the certified target coordinates directly. Frontend-v2 still needs a later
precision-aware display integration; no frontend change is included.

## Experimental protocol

The Oct 4 cohort has 791 targets (406 Portal, 385 Yapo); zero Portal targets have
timely geography in it. Two recoverable archived Portal points are not backdated
into that cohort. Current inventory coverage and benchmark coverage are distinct.
Targets are asking prices, not verified transactions; this previously studied
development cohort yields exploratory evidence only.

G3 grouped nested 3×3 CV uses two seeds; G1 is a grouping sensitivity. The grid
is tuned only in inner folds, with coverage at least A per source. Outer labels
are opened after all predictions. Errors use paired support; full coverage and
abstentions are separate. Portal falls back identically to A, so inner spatial
selection is effectively driven by Yapo despite the registered source weights.

A uses its original minimum 5 / maximum 20. Local profiles additionally limit
each reviewed dependency component to one training observation. This is an
experimental independence safeguard, not productive identity resolution; its
effect is bundled with spatial retrieval. Adaptive radii are .5/1/2/3/5 km,
with native physical filters, optional layout bands and native scoring/outliers.
Insufficient count or Neff returns exact A including its selected IDs.

Pre/post estimates, surface reference, contributing pool, adjustment magnitude,
direction and reason are retained. AM-frozen is attribution-only. If A lacks a
surface reference, that ablation abstains explicitly. The V2 amendment fixes that
mechanical case without changing the grid; failed V1 executions produced no
valid results. No weight optimization A1 was attempted.

## Reproduction (PowerShell, workspace root)

```powershell
$avmPython = 'work/avm-01-20261008/.venv-repro/Scripts/python.exe'
& $avmPython -B research/portal_geo_am_v0_20261010/run.py G3 20261009 fresh-reproduction --native-check
& $avmPython -B -c "import sys;sys.path.insert(0,'research/portal_geo_am_v0_20261010');from run import decrypt,HERE;assert decrypt(HERE/'fresh-reproduction.json.dpapi')==decrypt(HERE/'primary-v2.json.dpapi')"
& $avmPython -B research/portal_geo_am_v0_20261010/summarize.py
python -B -m pytest -c research/portal_geo_am_v0_20261010/pytest.ini research/portal_geo_am_v0_20261010/test_integration.py research/portal_geo_am_v0_20261010/test_recovery.py research/portal_geo_am_v0_20261010/legacy_tests -q -p no:cacheprovider
python -B -c "import sys;sys.path.insert(0,'work/avm-01-20261008/.venv-repro/Lib/site-packages');import pytest;raise SystemExit(pytest.main(['research/portal_geo_am_v0_20261010/test_am.py','-q','-p','no:cacheprovider']))"
```

Original runs and inputs must be present. Choose a fresh run tag; overwriting
predictions is refused. `summarize.py` checks the archived primary A, all 791
native predictions, the independent V2 repetition and immutable hashes.
`protocol.json` and `execution_seal_v2.json` lock original inputs and executables.

The patch requires review and integration approval. No production-ready claim
can be made for Portal spatial accuracy before a prospective geolocated cohort.
